 "layer_determination_of_the_R1430_residuals": {
  "class_A_start_side_265_plus_3": "ENGINE MEANS LAYER - fixed in this window (deterministic substitution + RED->GREEN).",
  "I2C2_SCL": "ENGINE MEANS LAYER but a DIFFERENT sub-cause, NOT fixed here: its pair is a port edge (the 9.3mm F.Cu stub at (51.5,56.6) IS the port) and the port -> U1.pad22 direction ALREADY ran, and EXHAUSTED with no path at all (no-path-coarse(exhausted-39316)). A start-side fix cannot help: the free space between the port and the pad is disconnected under the current clearance/window model. Named for the supervisor.",
  "I2C1_SDA": "DRAWING-LAYER CANDIDATE (sec.16.2) - NOT a maze edge at all: the final pair is a 0.6mm F.Cu stub at (51.5, 67.455) vs a 0.2mm B.Cu stub at (49.15, 62.505) = a layer-change/stitch on the frozen drawing side (the chain I2C1_SDA joint + D2 stitch). Per #K2-454 sec.2.6 the LAYER CALL belongs to the supervisor; ENG does NOT touch the frozen spec/drawing without approval.",
  "consequence": "fixing class A alone may not move C1=2: the two residuals sit one in the engine (a free-space disconnection) and one on the drawing side. Stated up front so the conditional run is not over-read."
 },
 "sec13_human_sentence": "Can the crew just connect it? YES for class A - the outside stub already ends ON the block edge, so the tool only has to be told \"start from that edge point\", not \"start from copper outside the fence\". For the two remaining wires the honest answer is NO, and this artifact names which trade each one needs.",
 "OWNER-ITEMS": 0
}